{
  "manufacturer": "eCharge Hardy Barth",
  "manufacturer_slug": "echarge-hardy-barth",
  "model": "eCharge EVCS (cPH2 / Salia controller), Modbus TCP map 2.3.0",
  "model_slug": "evcs-modbus-tcp-2-3",
  "short_model": "eCharge EVCS",
  "aliases": [
    "cPH2",
    "cPH22T22",
    "Hardy Barth Salia",
    "eCharge cPH2",
    "Hardy Barth wallbox"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "EV charger",
  "applies_to": "AC eCharge charging stations on firmware 2.5.2 or later, which report MapVersion 2.3.0; firmware 2.4.4-2.5.1 (MapVersion 2.0.0) has the same layout but different behaviour.",
  "summary": "eCharge Hardy Barth AC charging stations with the Salia controller run a Modbus TCP server on port 502 for EMS and SCADA control. Telemetry is in input registers, identity, configuration and control points in holding registers; floats and 32-bit values are big-endian with the high word first and need no scaling. Charging is controlled with a current target and a pause/allow register, with an optional heartbeat failsafe.",
  "transport": [
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Each row gives the 3xxxx/4xxxx number and the zero-based PDU address; PDU = register - 30001 (input) or - 40001 (holding). The manual's example frame 06 00 C9 00 10 writes 16 A to 40202 at PDU 201."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "2.5.2 (MapVersion 2.3.0)",
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus TCP Documentation",
    "doc_number": "Document version 2.3.0 (MapVersion 2.3.0)",
    "revision_date": "2026-11-05",
    "url": "https://docs.echarge.de/modbus-tcp/documentation.md",
    "pages": "Sections: Data representation and endianness; Addressing conventions; Register map overview; Enumerations; Controlling the charger; Entering (and leaving) failsafe"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Official documentation from eCharge's own docs site (markdown page).",
    "Word order: the manual states big-endian word order (high word at the lower address) and big-endian bytes for all multi-register values; values are already in engineering units (scale 1).",
    "Left out: Mains/Battery block 30501-30527 (the manual says this firmware does not populate it), StatusWord 30003 (reserved, always 0), ChargingInfo 30005 (free text, not for parsing), PhaseSwitchDelay/Duration 30305/30306 (the manual says they are unreliable), meter identity strings 41001-41024, and the accepted-but-ignored control registers 40201, 40205, 40207 and 40210-40225.",
    "Unused addresses read 0 without an exception, so a wrong function code or an off-by-one address returns zeros; read MapVersion (40001) first to check addressing.",
    "Other Unit IDs on the same IP: 2-4 forward to linked slave stations, and 100 (if enabled) is a Fronius-style SunSpec meter emulation starting with 'SunS' at 40001."
  ],
